{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"0c114bdd0a05fae2ba022adcdd6b63761b3d851a23fa03e9775e8b406e35d981","digest":{"component_or_area":"store compatibility record and fail-closed capability gate","key_entities":[".store-compat.json","src/rebar/_store/lock.py","src/rebar/_store/compat.py","src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","src/rebar/_commands/fsck_recover.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","StoreIncompatibleError","KNOWN_CAPABILITIES","check_store_compat()","describe_store_compat()","lock.acquire()","write_lock()"],"problem_keywords":["store compatibility","format version","required capabilities","fail-closed gate","forward compatibility","migration","rollback safety"],"propositions":["An old binary can omit unknown events during replay/compaction and emit stale state without a committed store-format version or required-capability record to fail closed, requiring v1.0 to define and enforce a store compatibility gate.","The gate must be inserted at the single convergence point for all lock-based store mutations—inside lock.acquire()—to cover write_lock() context-manager callers and direct acquire() callers (txn.py, compact.py, fsck.py:419) without enumeration.","An absent record (pre-v1.0 store) is treated as legacy format version 0 and passes through; an idempotent ensure unit writes the record when absent at init/fsck-repair/MCP-boot, and a missed ensure sweep does not block writes because the gate treats absent as pass-through.","A present but incompatible or corrupt record raises StoreIncompatibleError before any mutation, propagating to callers as non-zero exit, while read-only commands (fsck diagnostic, show, list, search) remain available with a machine-checkable compat_error object in fsck JSON output.","The gate must be un-swallowable on the ensure-sweep path via an explicit except StoreIncompatibleError: raise before run_ensures' broad exception handler, so init/MCP-boot/fsck-repair fail closed rather than silently completing.","Two paths without lock.acquire() (fsck_recover_cli raw-git mutations and reconcile._apply_mutations() Jira writes) require explicit check_store_compat() calls to close the gate coverage, and rollback safety is guaranteed because a pre-v1.0 binary ignores the unknown .store-compat.json file."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818453720409508,"uuid":"31cb63a9-e47e-4022-8176-b4f1f4e6e9c7"}